{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785260917,"nonce":"+im2cJ5cOT1tkK0SrIpri5IZIaw=","title":"ADR-0063 s2: move Step logs off the object store and onto the Data Depot","message":"`LogService::new(store, db)` takes a single `Arc\u003cdyn ObjectStore\u003e` — the **cold** store. With `SCARAB_S3_BUCKET` unset it falls back to `LocalDir(\"./.scarab/objects\")`, which on the Helm chart resolves inside the server Pod's `scratch` **emptyDir**. So logs die on every Pod roll and **nothing says so**: object storage is not merely a prerequisite, it is a silent one.\n\nAnd logs are the one data-plane class that **cannot be re-derived** — re-running a Step yields different logs. Cheapest class to keep, only class where loss is final.\n\n- [ ] Log bytes on the Depot's warm volume, keyed `{run, step, attempt}` + chunk sequence, **not** in the CAS (chunks are unique → no dedup; a hash per chunk buys nothing; the ordered offset index is still required)\n- [ ] Postgres keeps byte offsets only, bodies never (unchanged from ADR-0013)\n- [ ] **Live tail untouched** — the control plane still tails Pod stdout and broadcasts in-process for SSE; only the durable write redirects, and replay reads from the Depot\n- [ ] Evictable under pressure but **loud**: an Attempt whose logs were evicted says so in UI and API, never an empty pane (ADR-0027, smart never means mysterious)\n- [ ] Un-shipped chunks **pinned** against eviction while a durable sink exists; when the sink cannot keep up, eviction resumes and says so rather than filling the volume\n- [ ] External sinks (object store, Loki, VictoriaLogs) are **additional**, never the system of record\n- [ ] Logs get their own retention class + long TTL in the ADR-0050 sweeper, as Artifacts already have\n- [ ] The warm-size gauge's help text stops implying it measures only the CAS (folds in git-bug 1a9df08)","files":null}]}